@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<h1 class="mb-3">Privacy</h1>
<p class="lead text-muted mb-4">
    Syphonic is built for learners. This page is a concise statement you can evolve with legal counsel as you grow beyond a personal/educational project.
</p>

<div class="row g-4">
    <div class="col-lg-8">
        <section class="mb-5">
            <h2 class="h5">What we collect today</h2>
            <p>
                Signing in relies on ASP.NET Identity. Typical data includes email, password hashes, security stamps,
                lesson progress you generate by reading and completing lessons, and activity records that power your dashboard.
                When you browse without an account we do not persist personal identifiers beyond normal web server logs
                operated by whoever hosts your app.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section class="mb-5">
            <h2 class="h5">How we use information</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Account data saves your progress across sessions. Administrators can inspect accounts and unpublished lessons
                to curate geography content responsibly. Geography maps on the Maps lab may embed third-party imagery;
                consult their respective privacy policies before enabling classroom use.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h2 class="h5">Transparency &amp; control</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Learners manage credentials through the built-in “Manage account” page. Administrators should document any
                additional analytics or email providers before enabling them inside this codebase.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
    <aside class="col-lg-4">
        <div class="card border-0 bg-body-secondary shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="h6 mb-3">Operational reminder</h2>
                <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
                    Update this page when you integrate payments, telemetry, COPPA-compliant youth programs, marketing email,
                    or region-specific mandates.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </aside>
</div>
